WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.060
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book three.

2
00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:08.804
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.104 --> 00:00:15.216
Unit twenty-two: Growing Up. In this unit, you will talk about how you have changed as you grow up.

4
00:00:16.217 --> 00:00:17.102
Grow up.

5
00:00:17.802 --> 00:00:20.312
Grow up means to become older and become an adult.

6
00:00:20.612 --> 00:00:22.588
I want to be a pilot when I grow up.

7
00:00:23.288 --> 00:00:25.511
Your turn. Say: Grow up.

8
00:00:28.211 --> 00:00:29.050
Grow up.

9
00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:30.830
Change.

10
00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:33.217
Change means to become different.

11
00:00:33.517 --> 00:00:35.342
My hobbies have changed a lot.

12
00:00:36.042 --> 00:00:38.427
Your turn. Say: Change.

13
00:00:41.127 --> 00:00:41.896
Change.

14
00:00:42.883 --> 00:00:44.035
Responsible.

15
00:00:44.735 --> 00:00:47.873
Responsible means doing what you should do without being told.

16
00:00:48.173 --> 00:00:50.149
I have become more responsible at home.

17
00:00:50.849 --> 00:00:54.035
Your turn. Say: Responsible.

18
00:00:56.735 --> 00:00:57.806
Responsible.

19
00:00:58.817 --> 00:00:59.760
Independent.

20
00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:03.017
Independent means able to do things by yourself.

21
00:01:03.317 --> 00:01:06.050
I'm independent. I go to school by bike.

22
00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:09.611
Your turn. Say: Independent.

23
00:01:12.311 --> 00:01:13.405
Independent.

24
00:01:14.417 --> 00:01:15.302
Teenager.

25
00:01:16.002 --> 00:01:19.580
Teenager means a person between thirteen and nineteen years old.

26
00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:21.497
My brother is a teenager.

27
00:01:22.197 --> 00:01:24.547
Your turn. Say: Teenager.

28
00:01:27.247 --> 00:01:28.086
Teenager.

29
00:01:29.083 --> 00:01:30.026
Choices.

30
00:01:30.726 --> 00:01:32.830
Choices means things you decide to do.

31
00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:35.455
As we grow, we make our own choices.

32
00:01:36.155 --> 00:01:38.784
Your turn. Say: Choices.

33
00:01:41.484 --> 00:01:42.416
Choices.

34
00:01:43.417 --> 00:01:44.325
Future.

35
00:01:45.025 --> 00:01:47.059
Future means the time that will come.

36
00:01:47.359 --> 00:01:49.150
I'm excited about my future.

37
00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:52.549
Your turn. Say: Future.

38
00:01:55.249 --> 00:01:56.006
Future.

39
00:01:57.017 --> 00:01:57.878
Proud.

40
00:01:58.578 --> 00:02:01.158
Proud means happy about something you or others did.

41
00:02:01.458 --> 00:02:03.005
My parents are proud of me.

42
00:02:03.705 --> 00:02:06.334
Your turn. Say: Proud.

43
00:02:09.034 --> 00:02:09.896
Proud.

44
00:02:10.883 --> 00:02:12.906
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:13.206 --> 00:02:15.984
Sreypich, how have you changed since last year?

46
00:02:17.283 --> 00:02:19.120
I have become more independent.

47
00:02:20.417 --> 00:02:22.230
What can you do by yourself now?

48
00:02:23.517 --> 00:02:26.851
I have learned to cook rice, and I have started riding my bike to school.

49
00:02:28.150 --> 00:02:29.836
Your parents must be proud!

50
00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:34.069
Yes! I have become more responsible too.

51
00:02:35.383 --> 00:02:39.206
Grammar focus: Present perfect (I have become).

52
00:02:39.506 --> 00:02:41.110
I have become more independent.

53
00:02:41.410 --> 00:02:44.919
Use the present perfect to talk about changes from the past until now.

54
00:02:45.917 --> 00:02:48.453
Now read and listen. I'm Growing Up.

55
00:02:48.753 --> 00:02:51.704
I'm twelve years old, and I have changed a lot.

56
00:02:53.017 --> 00:02:56.375
I have grown taller, and I have become more independent.

57
00:02:57.683 --> 00:03:00.379
I have learned to wash my clothes and help my mum cook.

58
00:03:01.683 --> 00:03:04.844
Soon I will be a teenager, and I will make more choices.

59
00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:09.380
My parents are proud because I have become more responsible.

60
00:03:10.683 --> 00:03:13.208
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:13.508 --> 00:03:15.554
I blank become more responsible.

62
00:03:15.854 --> 00:03:19.020
A, have. B, has. C, am.

63
00:03:23.017 --> 00:03:25.028
The answer is A: have.

64
00:03:26.517 --> 00:03:28.760
Able to do things by yourself is blank.

65
00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:33.015
A, independent. B, responsible. C, tired.

66
00:03:37.017 --> 00:03:39.423
The answer is A: independent.

67
00:03:40.917 --> 00:03:43.532
A person between thirteen and nineteen is a blank.

68
00:03:43.832 --> 00:03:47.183
A, teenager. B, baby. C, grandparent.

69
00:03:51.183 --> 00:03:53.229
The answer is A: teenager.

70
00:03:54.717 --> 00:03:58.565
Now it's your turn to speak. How have you changed as you grow up?

71
00:04:03.865 --> 00:04:09.617
I have become more responsible. I have learned to cook, and I have started going to school by myself.

72
00:04:09.917 --> 00:04:11.696
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:12.683 --> 00:04:17.054
Great work today! You learned eight new words and present perfect (i have become).

74
00:04:17.354 --> 00:04:22.154
Today's value is maturity. Take responsibility for your choices as you grow.

75
00:04:22.454 --> 00:04:25.443
See you in Unit twenty-three. Goodbye!

76
00:04:25.743 --> 00:04:28.372
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

